# The @visiolab scope lives on GitHub Packages, not npmjs.com. This mapping is
# needed before `pnpm version` as well as before `pnpm publish`: the release plan
# asks the registry whether name@currentVersion already exists, and a 401 is
# indistinguishable from "never published" — which silently suppresses bumps.
#
# The token is not here on purpose. pnpm will not expand env vars in credentials
# read from a committed .npmrc. CI gets it from setup-vp's registry-url input;
# locally, set it once with a PAT that has read:packages:
#
#   pnpm config set "//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken" <token>
@visiolab:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
